# Learned: test-authoring

Auto-maintained by the `agents-memory-updater` subagent. New bullets are
capped at 200 chars and 12 bullets per section. The existing entries below
were harvested verbatim from `AGENTS.md` during the one-time context
cleanup; they may exceed the 200-char cap.

## Learned User Preferences

- Write failing tests first (TDD), then fix to pass; preserve existing tests; make minimal, targeted changes and run typecheck before considering done; remove tests for non-shipped APIs/behaviors rather than skipping them; do not mock Radix `Collapsible`/portal-rendered components in jsdom — find and fix the real reason the test sees the wrong initial state instead of mocking around it
- In negative type tests, pass a deliberately wrong-typed value via `// @ts-expect-error`, not `as unknown as`; positive cases call the method directly on a real fixture so typechecking stays intact.
- Delete model-specific or order-dependent chat SSE integration assertions (usage-metadata counts, preamble-skipping `text-start`) — non-deterministic tests must not ship.
- GeoSpec recursive discovery is runner-owned, not inferred from lazy chat file-tree context; multi-file GeoSpec runs stay serial unless worker pooling is explicitly designed.
- GeoSpec tests use `loadModel({ file })` or `{ code, file }`; do not pass public kernel hints. Fix runtime inference/diagnostics for ambiguity.
- GeoSpec triangle-heavy matcher math belongs in the canonical native/WASM backend; JS is orchestration, diagnostics, or experiments only.
- GeoSpec load paths keep rich mesh diagnostics lazy, dedupe `loadModel()` per invocation, and reuse scoped runtimes; never reintroduce eager connected-piece stats.
- Spec-first tau-examples land geospec suites RED first (the red rows are the modeling work queue); the runtime-e2e green gate is added only once the model iterates to green — never alongside the red suites.
- GeoSpec wall-thickness reads corner-fillet CHORDS (a plan fillet of radius r measures ≈ r·√2) and fillet-to-seam ledges as minimum walls: square off small printed features near the wall floor, or size fillets so r·√2 clears it. Interference relationship rows need explicit `maxVolume` (closed band); vendored hardware dims are MEASURED from occurrence bounds, never assumed from nominal specs.
- Byte-locked `toMatchFileSnapshot` artifacts (e.g. geospec `__evidence-snapshots__/*.json`) must be formatter-exempt: vitest 4 NEVER prettifies file snapshots, so a repo `oxfmt`/format pass rewriting them breaks byte parity with whitespace-only diffs. Root `.prettierignore` covers oxfmt (it reads `.gitignore` + `.prettierignore` natively); the alternative is a formatter-stable serializer (the UI `__shader-snapshots__` compact-array helper), which silently breaks once any emitted line exceeds the formatter's print width.

## Learned Workspace Facts

- ConfigModule snapshots `process.env` at IMPORT time: integration tests must pin env in `vi.hoisted` in the test file — the app-factory `env` option is too late (symptom: Stripe webhook 400 FAILED_TO_CONSTRUCT_STRIPE_EVENT).
- `ioredis-mock` shares ONE keyspace per process regardless of `{data:{}}` — harnesses must `await redis.flushall()` at creation or residual keys leak across tests.
- `mockDeep<DatabaseService>` covers `query.*.find*` but does NOT fabricate drizzle fluent chains — stub `update().set().where()` explicitly when the code under test uses builders.
- Matchers like `expect.stringMatching`/`expect.any` inside `objectContaining` property positions trip `no-unsafe-assignment` — assert those fields via literal `toHaveBeenCalledWith` values or a typed `mock.calls[0]?.[0]` cast instead.
- A scripted `BaseChatModel` must implement `_streamResponseChunks` (yield `AIMessageChunk`s) to surface reasoning/text UI parts: `@ai-sdk/langchain`'s `toUIMessageStream` only extracts `{type:'reasoning'}`/text content from `AIMessageChunk`s, so a `_generate`-only model streams its `tool_calls` (structural) but drops reasoning/text. Derive the replay step from the assistant-message count (`messages.filter(m => m.type === 'ai').length`), never `instanceof AIMessage` (fails across class-identity boundaries → step stuck at 0 → `GraphRecursionError`) and never `getType()` (lint-deprecated; use `.type`).
- `createTestApp`'s headless RPC dispatcher passes tool paths straight to the raw virtual fs (no project-mount resolution), so scripted tool-call args AND `memFs.writeFile`/`readFile` must use project-root-absolute paths (`/main.scad`, not `main.scad`); `readFile` needs the `'utf8'` arg or it returns a `Uint8Array`. Integration tests under `app/testing/**` run only via `vitest.integration.config.ts` (the default `test` target excludes that dir).
